.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt OPEN 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm open
.Nd open a scheme-routed file or scheme
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x61).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
routes a path of the form
.Dq scheme:suffix
to the server registered for
.Va scheme .
Normally a successful reply creates and returns a new SchemeFile handle.
.Pp
A server may instead set the reply flag
.Dv REPLY_HANDLE
and provide exactly one attachment (see
.Xr send 2 ) .
In that form,
.Nm
returns the transferred client-table attachment directly and discards the provisional SchemeFile
handle.  Subsequent operations apply to the returned object; they are not routed through the
opening scheme server.
.Pp
The attachment must be transferable by the replying server.  Its rights are reduced by the
attachment rights mask, with a zero mask retaining all of the server's current rights.
.Sh OPEN FLAGS
The protocol
.Va flags
word is a 16-bit wire bit set, not the Linux
.Vt O_*
numbering.
.Bl -tag -width WIRE_OPEN_NOFOLLOW -offset indent
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_READ
Read access; set for
.Dv O_RDONLY
and for the read half of
.Dv O_RDWR .
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_WRITE
Write access; set for
.Dv O_WRONLY
and for the write half of
.Dv O_RDWR .
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_CREATE
Create a missing regular file.
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_EXCL
Require
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_CREATE
and fail with
.Er EEXIST
when the path exists.  The test and the create are one server operation.
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_TRUNC
Truncate a regular file to zero length.  Requires write access and is
incompatible with
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_DIRECTORY .
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_APPEND
Place every write at the current end of the file.  Requires write access and
is atomic at the server.
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_DIRECTORY
Require the resolved path to be a directory; a non-directory returns
.Er ENOTDIR .
.It Dv WIRE_OPEN_NOFOLLOW
Fail with
.Er ELOOP
when the final component is a symbolic link.  Intermediate links are still
followed.
.El
.Pp
At least one of
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_READ
and
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_WRITE
is required.  Unknown bits and invalid combinations are rejected with
.Er EINVAL .
A creation with
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_CREATE
uses mode
.Li 0o644
(0o666 masked by the server umask 0o022); use
.Xr chmod 2
to change it.
.Pp
The kernel carries all eight wire bits, rejects unknown bits with
.Er EINVAL ,
and derives the new handle's
.Dv READ / WRITE / DUP / TRANSFER
rights from the access bits only.  Combination checks and the atomic
.Dv O_EXCL / O_APPEND / O_TRUNC
operations are the server's.  The successful reply's server file id (the
.Va server_cookie )
is used as the wire
.Va file_id
for every later request on the handle; the handle itself is transferable.
.Sh PATHS
An absolute path is normalized by
.Nm vfsd :
repeated separators and
.Ql .\&
components are removed,
.Ql ..\&
pops the previous component, and
.Ql ..\&
above
.Pa /
is
.Er EINVAL .
A trailing slash or a final
.Ql .\&
or
.Ql ..\&
requires the result to be a directory; a trailing slash on a regular file is
.Er ENOTDIR .
Servers receive the path relative to their mount root and must reject
.Ql .\&
and
.Ql ..\&
components.
.Sh FILES
The open-file description, cursor and reference count are server state.  A
successful
.Xr dup 2
shares them; the server releases the description only at the last
.Xr close 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
A non-negative SchemeFile handle on success.  The protocol status is a positive
errno on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er -offset indent
.It Er EINVAL
Unknown or invalid open flags, or an invalid path.
.It Er ENOENT
A path component does not exist.
.It Er ENOTDIR
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_DIRECTORY
or a trailing slash named a non-directory.
.It Er EEXIST
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_CREATE | WIRE_OPEN_EXCL
and the path exists.
.It Er ELOOP
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_NOFOLLOW
found a final symbolic link, or too many links were followed.
.It Er EISDIR
Write or truncate was requested on a directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr dup 2 ,
.Xr fstat 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
